<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="TradeMe Category Details - Performance Test" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Performance test for the Trade Me sandbox Categories Details API.

Requirement traceability (see README.md):
NFR-01 - VUsers (threads) equal half the number of Category IDs in testdata/category_ids.csv
NFR-02 - Ramp-up at one VUser per second
NFR-03 - Exactly 10 API calls in total across the 1-minute steady state
NFR-04 - 90th percentile response time at most 500 ms

All execution parameters are overridable through JMeter properties (pass -J on the
CLI or use scripts/run-test.ps1, which is the recommended entry point):
  -Jthreads=5          VUser count              (default 5)
  -Jrampup=5           ramp-up seconds          (default 5 = 1 VUser per second)
  -Jsteady_state=60    steady state seconds     (default 60)
  -Jthroughput=10      total calls per minute   (default 10)
  -Jprotocol / -Jhost / -Jport / -JoutputDir / -JtestDataPath

Design note (NFR-03): the CSV Data Set consumes one Category ID per API call with
recycling disabled, and an IfController guard skips any iteration once the data
set is exhausted. The Constant Throughput Timer paces those calls at the
configured rate, so each run performs exactly one call per Category ID:
total calls = min(loops x threads, number of Category IDs).
scripts/run-test.ps1 derives loops = ceil(CategoryIdCount / threads) + 1 so every
ID is called exactly once. The loop count is finite by design: an always-false
IfController as the direct child of an infinite thread group triggers unbounded
controller recursion (StackOverflowError) in JMeter 5.6.x.</stringProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.functional_mode">false</boolProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.tearDown_on_shutdown">true</boolProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.serialize_threadgroups">false</boolProp>
      <elementProp name="TestPlan.user_defined_variables" elementType="Arguments" guiclass="ArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments" testname="User Defined Variables" enabled="true">
        <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
          <elementProp name="protocol" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">protocol</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(protocol,https)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="host" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">host</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(host,api.tmsandbox.co.nz)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="port" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">port</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(port,)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="outputDir" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">outputDir</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(outputDir,./results)}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
        </collectionProp>
      </elementProp>
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.user_define_classpath"></stringProp>
    </TestPlan>
    <hashTree>
      <ConfigTestElement guiclass="HttpDefaultsGui" testclass="ConfigTestElement" testname="HTTP Request Defaults" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.domain">${host}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.port">${port}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.protocol">${protocol}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.connect_timeout">10000</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.response_timeout">30000</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments" guiclass="HTTPArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments" testname="User Defined Variables" enabled="true">
          <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments"/>
        </elementProp>
      </ConfigTestElement>
      <hashTree/>
      <CSVDataSet guiclass="TestBeanGUI" testclass="CSVDataSet" testname="Category IDs (Test Data)" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="filename">${__P(testDataPath,./testdata)}/category_ids.csv</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="fileEncoding">UTF-8</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="variableNames">categoryId</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ignoreFirstLine">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="delimiter">,</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="quotedData">false</boolProp>
        <boolProp name="recycle">false</boolProp>
        <boolProp name="stopThread">false</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="shareMode">shareMode.all</stringProp>
      </CSVDataSet>
      <hashTree/>
      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup" testname="Category Details Load (NFR-01 and NFR-02)" enabled="true">
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_error">continue</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="ThreadGroup.main_controller" elementType="LoopController" guiclass="LoopControlPanel" testclass="LoopController" testname="Loop Controller" enabled="true">
          <boolProp name="LoopController.continue_forever">false</boolProp>
          <stringProp name="LoopController.loops">${__P(loops,2)}</stringProp>
        </elementProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">${__P(threads,5)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">${__P(rampup,5)}</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.scheduler">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.duration">${__P(steady_state,60)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.delay">0</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.same_user_on_next_iteration">true</boolProp>
      </ThreadGroup>
      <hashTree>
        <ConstantThroughputTimer guiclass="TestBeanGUI" testclass="ConstantThroughputTimer" testname="Throughput Pacing (NFR-03)" enabled="true">
          <intProp name="calcMode">1</intProp>
          <stringProp name="throughput">${__P(throughput,10)}</stringProp>
        </ConstantThroughputTimer>
        <hashTree/>
        <IfController guiclass="IfControllerPanel" testclass="IfController" testname="Guard - stop when test data exhausted" enabled="true">
          <stringProp name="IfController.condition">${__jexl3("${categoryId}" != "&lt;EOF&gt;")}</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="IfController.useExpression">true</boolProp>
          <boolProp name="IfController.evaluateAll">false</boolProp>
        </IfController>
        <hashTree>
          <HTTPSamplerProxy guiclass="HttpTestSampleGui" testclass="HTTPSamplerProxy" testname="GET Category Details" enabled="true">
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.postBodyRaw">false</boolProp>
            <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments" guiclass="HTTPArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments" testname="User Defined Variables" enabled="true">
              <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
                <elementProp name="catalogue" elementType="HTTPArgument">
                  <boolProp name="HTTPArgument.always_encode">false</boolProp>
                  <stringProp name="Argument.value">false</stringProp>
                  <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
                  <boolProp name="HTTPArgument.use_equals">true</boolProp>
                  <stringProp name="Argument.name">catalogue</stringProp>
                </elementProp>
              </collectionProp>
            </elementProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.domain"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.port"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.protocol"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.contentEncoding"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.path">/v1/Categories/${categoryId}/Details.json</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.method">GET</stringProp>
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.follow_redirects">true</boolProp>
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.auto_redirects">false</boolProp>
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.use_keepalive">true</boolProp>
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.DO_MULTIPART_POST">false</boolProp>
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.BROWSER_COMPATIBLE_MULTIPART">false</boolProp>
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.image_parser">false</boolProp>
            <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.concurrentDwn">false</boolProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.concurrentPool">6</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.embedded_url_re"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.connect_timeout"></stringProp>
            <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.response_timeout"></stringProp>
          </HTTPSamplerProxy>
          <hashTree>
            <HeaderManager guiclass="HeaderPanel" testclass="HeaderManager" testname="HTTP Headers" enabled="true">
              <collectionProp name="HeaderManager.headers">
                <elementProp name="" elementType="Header">
                  <stringProp name="Header.name">Accept</stringProp>
                  <stringProp name="Header.value">application/json</stringProp>
                </elementProp>
                <elementProp name="" elementType="Header">
                  <stringProp name="Header.name">User-Agent</stringProp>
                  <stringProp name="Header.value">JMeter-PerformanceTest/1.0</stringProp>
                </elementProp>
              </collectionProp>
            </HeaderManager>
            <hashTree/>
            <JSR223Assertion guiclass="TestBeanGUI" testclass="JSR223Assertion" testname="Functional Assertions - status, CategoryId, CanRelist (Groovy)" enabled="true">
              <stringProp name="cacheKey">true</stringProp>
              <stringProp name="filename"></stringProp>
              <stringProp name="parameters"></stringProp>
              <stringProp name="script"><![CDATA[
import groovy.json.JsonSlurper

// Functional validation for one API response (assignment Functional Requirements).
// Bound variables provided by JMeter:
//   SampleResult     - the sampler result for this API call
//   AssertionResult  - this assertion, used to report failures
//   vars             - JMeter variables; 'categoryId' comes from the CSV Data Set
//   log              - JMeter logger

def sample = SampleResult
def assertion = AssertionResult
def requestedCategoryId = vars.get('categoryId')

// The CSV Data Set writes the literal string '<EOF>' into the variables once the
// test data is exhausted (recycling is disabled). Nothing to validate then.
if (requestedCategoryId == null || requestedCategoryId == '<EOF>') {
    return
}

// ---- Check 1: response status must be HTTP 200 ------------------------------
def statusCode = sample.getResponseCode()
if (!'200'.equals(statusCode)) {
    assertion.setFailure(true)
    assertion.setFailureMessage('Response status check failed - expected HTTP 200 but received ' +
            statusCode + ' for CategoryId=' + requestedCategoryId)
    return
}

// ---- Parse the response body as JSON ----------------------------------------
def body = sample.getResponseDataAsString()
def json
try {
    json = new JsonSlurper().parseText(body)
} catch (Exception parseError) {
    assertion.setFailure(true)
    assertion.setFailureMessage('Response body is not valid JSON for CategoryId=' +
            requestedCategoryId + ' - ' + parseError.getMessage())
    return
}

// ---- Check 2: parameter check - returned CategoryId must match the request ---
def returnedCategoryId = (json.CategoryId == null) ? '' : String.valueOf(json.CategoryId)
if (!requestedCategoryId.equals(returnedCategoryId)) {
    assertion.setFailure(true)
    assertion.setFailureMessage('CategoryId parameter check failed - expected ' +
            requestedCategoryId + ' but the API returned ' + returnedCategoryId)
    return
}

// ---- Check 3: text check - CanRelist must be true ----------------------------
// Note: on the live sandbox, Category 6331 currently returns CanRelist=false.
// This call is intentionally marked as failed - it is a data finding that is
// documented in README.md and in the performance test report.
if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(json.CanRelist)) {
    assertion.setFailure(true)
    assertion.setFailureMessage('CanRelist text check failed - expected [true] but was [' +
            json.CanRelist + '] for CategoryId=' + requestedCategoryId)
}
]]></stringProp>
              <stringProp name="scriptLanguage">groovy</stringProp>
            </JSR223Assertion>
            <hashTree/>
            <JSR223PostProcessor guiclass="TestBeanGUI" testclass="JSR223PostProcessor" testname="CSV Writer - CategoryId, Name, Path, PromotionId, Price (Groovy)" enabled="true">
              <stringProp name="cacheKey">true</stringProp>
              <stringProp name="filename"></stringProp>
              <stringProp name="parameters"></stringProp>
              <stringProp name="script"><![CDATA[
import groovy.json.JsonSlurper

// Writes the assignment CSV deliverable: one row per Promotion.
// Columns: CategoryId, Name, Path, PromotionId, Price
// Category-level fields (Name, Path) are repeated on every promotion row so the
// file stays self-contained when it is sorted or filtered.
// Bound variables provided by JMeter: prev (the SampleResult), vars, props, log.

def sample = prev
if (sample == null || !'200'.equals(sample.getResponseCode())) {
    return // only successful HTTP responses contribute rows
}

def requestedCategoryId = vars.get('categoryId')
if (requestedCategoryId == null || requestedCategoryId == '<EOF>') {
    return
}

def json
try {
    json = new JsonSlurper().parseText(sample.getResponseDataAsString())
} catch (Exception parseError) {
    log.warn('CSV writer - response body was not valid JSON for CategoryId=' + requestedCategoryId)
    return
}

// Minimal RFC 4180 quoting for fields that may contain commas or quotes.
def csvEscape = { value ->
    def s = (value == null) ? '' : String.valueOf(value)
    if (s.indexOf(',') >= 0 || s.indexOf('"') >= 0 || s.indexOf('\n') >= 0 || s.indexOf('\r') >= 0) {
        s = '"' + s.replace('"', '""') + '"'
    }
    return s
}

def categoryName = csvEscape(json.Name)
def categoryPath = csvEscape(json.Path)

def rows = new StringBuilder()
def promotions = json.Promotions
if (promotions == null || promotions.isEmpty()) {
    rows.append(csvEscape(requestedCategoryId)).append(',').append(categoryName).append(',').append(categoryPath)
            .append(',').append(',').append(System.lineSeparator())
} else {
    promotions.each { promotion ->
        rows.append(csvEscape(requestedCategoryId)).append(',').append(categoryName).append(',').append(categoryPath)
                .append(',').append(csvEscape(promotion.Id)).append(',').append(csvEscape(promotion.Price))
                .append(System.lineSeparator())
    }
}

def outputDir = new File(vars.get('outputDir'))
if (!outputDir.exists()) {
    outputDir.mkdirs()
}
def csvFile = new File(outputDir, 'category_promotions.csv')

// Serialise file writes across VUsers with a lock shared through JMeter properties.
def lock = props.get('csv.writer.lock')
if (lock == null) {
    lock = new Object()
    props.put('csv.writer.lock', lock)
}
synchronized (lock) {
    if (!csvFile.exists()) {
        csvFile.setText('CategoryId,Name,Path,PromotionId,Price' + System.lineSeparator(), 'UTF-8')
    }
    csvFile.append(rows.toString(), 'UTF-8')
}
]]></stringProp>
              <stringProp name="scriptLanguage">groovy</stringProp>
            </JSR223PostProcessor>
            <hashTree/>
          </hashTree>
        </hashTree>
      </hashTree>
    </hashTree>
  </hashTree>
</jmeterTestPlan>
